$ feov-record 
exit 2
stderr:
feov-record: you named no command, so nothing ran. The commands below are the whole surface.

feov-record — the seat-side record runtime (the verb set IS the role boundary)

A lens structurally cannot mint or close a board gap: no such verb exists in its
namespace. Blue has no board verbs at all. The bench rules and never originates.

Usage:
  feov-record [flags]
  feov-record [command]

Available Commands:
  bench        the bench — opinions, halt, certification. Never originates. It rules petitions through `motion petition rule`.
  blue         blue seats — revisions, manifest rows, directions. No board verbs at all. To contest a grade or petition the bench, see `motion`.
  capture      run /research's post-hoc capture auditor (operator; nine audits + cost.md/tarball/scorecards)
  completion   Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  count-claims count the FOOTNOTED declarative claims in blue's report (read-only)
  dashboard    render a run's live dashboard.html (operator; board/cost/seats/judiciary/scorecards)
  fetch        cached, hash-verified web read (replaces WebFetch); serves both sides the same bytes
  friction     read the run's friction channel (operator; every capability gap a seat reported, and every seat that reported none)
  graph        render a run's actual behaviour (seat flow + gap lifecycle) as mermaid or dot (read-only)
  help         Help about any command
  hook         PreToolUse/PostToolUse backends for the blue-report lockdown (invoked by hooks.json, not a seat verb)
  lens         red lens seats — findings, source verification, proof re-runs. Cannot mint or close a gap: that is the merge's.
  merge        the red merge seat — the board's only writer.
  motion       file and rule on a motion — a grade dispute, a petition, or a ruling on a direction. One mechanism, one id.
  scorecard    print a chair's scorecard for this run (operator; the seat's in-run self-read)
  setup        build a research run's blackboard: skeleton, pins, memory mirrors, and the .run-live marker (operator; writes files)
  verify       cross-check a run's record against its invariants, and tally it (read-only)

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for feov-record
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace
  -v, --version          version for feov-record

Use "feov-record [command] --help" for more information about a command.

