$ feov-record lens help
exit 0
stdout:
red lens seats — findings, source verification, proof re-runs. Cannot mint or close a gap: that is the merge's.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record lens [flags]
  feov-record lens [command]

Available Commands:
  finding     a lens finding (the tool assigns the L{role}-F{N} label): --key <your local F1> --severity <g> --likelihood <g> --impact <g> --reason "..." --location "<the exact sentence, quoted from the report and nothing else>". THE CHANNEL FOR ANY DEFECT IN THE TEXT, including the ones the evidence verbs cannot reach: a claim resting on NO citation and no proof, an assertion whose source you cannot obtain, a figure with no derivation. `verify` and `reproduce` judge evidence that EXISTS; this raises the claim that has none.
  friction    a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  register    FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  reproduce   re-RUN a proof AND READ IT: --id <sha256> --as sound|unsound --reason "<what the script actually computes>" — the tool records whether it REPRODUCED; you judge whether it PROVES the claim
  show        read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry
  verify      adjudicate ONE citation: --anchor c-<hex> (from `show evidence`) or --independent, --claim "..." --as supports|refutes|absent|… --confidence high|medium|low --reason "<what the source actually says>". THIS VERB JUDGES A CITATION THAT EXISTS. A claim carrying NO citation at all is not verified as `absent` — `absent` means you read the source and the claim is not in it. An UNEVIDENCED claim is a finding: raise it with `finding`, which is the channel for "this assertion rests on nothing", exactly as it is for any other defect in the text.

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for lens

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record lens [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record merge help
exit 0
stdout:
the red merge seat — the board's only writer.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record merge [flags]
  feov-record merge [command]

Available Commands:
  close           close a gap WITH its verification anchor: --id R2-3 --as closed|closed_with_regression|... (--anchor-seat L1 --anchor-tool "git show" --anchor-target "7bc501e:path" | --carried-from <round>) [--successor R3-1] --reason "<what was verified and why it holds>"
  closing         a ### RED CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  inquiry-support your per-round verdict that the REPORT still carries a line of inquiry: --id Q1 --as supported|weakened|unsupported|absent --reason "<what the report says for it, quoted>". Read the report ONCE this round and vote every line against that read
  mint            mint a board gap (id is TOOL-assigned; --key <stable-label> makes retries idempotent): --class <slug>|--class-new <slug> --definition --neighbor --distinguisher, --location "..." --problem "..."|--reason --fix "..." --check "<acceptance check red runs at re-audit>" --severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade> [--supersedes R1-2,R1-7] [--found-by L5-F3,L6-F2]
  near-match      screen a candidate against the board before minting: --candidate "<problem text>" [--location "<section>"] — returns the top 5 gaps (open AND closed) by lexical overlap, so a near-duplicate surfaces as a reopen (mint --supersedes <id>) rather than a fresh gap. The tool SCREENS and ranks; you decide reopen-or-new. Read-only: it records nothing.
  position        the round's ### RED section (prose via --reason)
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  regrade         same-id grade movement, recorded with its reason: --id R2-5 [--severity/--likelihood/--impact/--cx <grade>] --reason "..."
  show            read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry
  spot-check      the round archive spot-check record (W1.8 duty): --ids R1-4,R2-7 [--notes "..."] | --none --reason "..." when the archive was empty at round start
  verdict         the seat's terminal act: --as PASS|FAIL — checkpoints records/ to the recovery mirror

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for merge

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record merge [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record blue help
exit 0
stdout:
blue seats — revisions, manifest rows, directions. No board verbs at all. To contest a grade or petition the bench, see `motion`.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record blue [flags]
  feov-record blue [command]

Available Commands:
  cite            cite a source at a quoted sentence — the tool fetches, caches, and splices an invisible immortal anchor; you never type a footnote: --location "<the exact sentence, quoted from the report and nothing else — NOT a heading plus a sentence, it is matched literally>" --url <u> --title <t> [--claim "..."] [--key <your C1>]
  claim-index     locate every site of each FOOTNOTED claim in your report (read-only)
  closing         a ### BLUE CLOSING entry per docketed gap: --id <gap> --reason <prose>
  edit            replace an exact span in blue/report.md, preserving red's finding-markers: --key <your F1> --old "<exact current span>" --new "<replacement>" --reason "..."
  friction        a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  line-of-inquiry PROPOSE a line of inquiry (--line "<approach>" --hypothesis "<what would be true if it pays off>" [--status] [--method]; the tool assigns its id), or MOVE one you already proposed (--id A1 --status proposed|pursued|declined|abandoned --reason "<what changed>")
  manifest-row    one correctness-manifest receipt per repaired gap: --id R2-3 --row "figures recomputed; acceptance check run: pass; sites swept: S2,S4"
  position        the round's ### BLUE section (prose via --reason)
  prove           settle a claim by COMPUTING it: --location "<the exact sentence>" --script <path under the run dir> [--cites <the method's citation label>] — the tool runs it twice, caches the script and its output, and splices an invisible proof anchor at that sentence
  register        FIRST ACTION at the seat: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  retire          remove a claim from the report, on the record: --claim "<the claim, quoted>" --reason "..." [--superseded-by "<the claim that replaces it>"]
  revision        the round record itself (--reason carries what changed this round) — singleton per seat-round; emit AFTER your report edits land
  show            read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for blue

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

Use "feov-record blue [command] --help" for more information about a command.

$ feov-record bench help
exit 0
stdout:
the bench — opinions, halt, certification. Never originates. It rules petitions through `motion petition rule`.

If you need a verb or a flag that is not listed here, it does not exist for you:
do not improvise around it, and do not hand-write the artifact. Record what you
needed and what you would have done with the 'friction' verb — a missing
capability is a finding about the tooling, and that channel is how it gets fixed.

Usage:
  feov-record bench [flags]
  feov-record bench [command]

Available Commands:
  assemble    assemble <run>/report.md from the record — blue's audited sections lifted verbatim, the rest composed from the event log; no inputs
  certify     the run-end certification statement ("what I would want a human to re-examine"): --reason <statement>
  declare     state a holding that binds how the record is READ without moving any gap: --reason "<the construction, correction or holding>"
  friction    a capability gap or protocol misfit, as an event that survives aborts: --reason. CLOSE THIS CHANNEL EVERY SITTING: --none --reason "<what you reached for and found>" says nothing blocked you, which silence cannot say — an empty friction log reads the same whether the sitting was clean or the channel went unused
  halt        the safety boundary: --reason <written opinion — capture relays it like a FAIL, never smoothed>
  opinion     a ruling as an OPINION: --id R3-2 --as carried|closed|... --principle "..." --tension "correctness vs economy" --review-flag "why a human should look" --reason <rationale>
  outcome     record the run's terminal verdict as a fact: --as VERIFIED|CEILING|HALTED|UNVERIFIED --reason "<how the run ended, in your words>" [--deadlocked] [--exhausted]
  register    FIRST ACTION at the sitting: `register`, with no flags — the engine injects your run and your identity, and a --run or --seat-id that disagrees with the dispatch is refused rather than obeyed
  show        read a projection on STDOUT (the tool is the read path; the .md files are for human verification). With no projection named, you get YOUR PENDING WORK: report | board | findings | worklist | motions | debate | changes | evidence | lines-of-inquiry | telemetry

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for bench

Global Flags:
      --json             emit a structured JSON result (and structured errors) instead of human text
      --run string       the run directory. REQUIRED unless the engine injected it — it does in a real run, which is why you rarely type it. A value that DISAGREES with the run you were dispatched into is refused rather than obeyed
      --seat-id string   your seat id, assigned by the engine and bound to this role's namespace

